  "summary": "The King of Fighters '94 is SNK's crossover fighting game, first released for Neo Geo MVS on 25 August 1994.",
  "body": [
    "The King of Fighters '94 is SNK's crossover fighting game, first released for Neo Geo MVS on 25 August 1994. It brings characters from Fatal Fury, Art of Fighting, Ikari Warriors and Psycho Soldier into a tournament alongside new fighters led by Kyo Kusanagi. Three-member teams replace the usual isolated contestant, giving the event a broader cast and another layer of preparation. The tournament's organiser, Rugal Bernstein, supplies the final threat. Its success established an annual series that would become one of SNK's central identities in the arcade.",
    "The player chooses one of eight fixed teams, then decides the order in which its members will fight. A defeated character gives way to the next teammate, while the winner remains with a small amount of health restored. The match ends when one side loses all three members. That continuity makes the opening fighter's performance matter to everybody following them. A strong first round can remove an opponent and leave another rival facing a weakened but still dangerous character, turning a succession of duels into one extended team contest.",
    "Four attack buttons distinguish light and strong punches and kicks. The power gauge grows through defensive exchanges and damage, and can also be charged manually, although doing so leaves the fighter exposed. Filling it strengthens attacks temporarily and enables a powerful special move. Teammates waiting at the edge can also assist under the appropriate conditions, making their presence more than decorative. The combination gives the crossover a shared structure: familiar characters bring their own techniques, while the gauge and team order make them part of the same tactical contest."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "SNK brings its fighters together",
    "Choosing the order of the team",
    "Power with a moment of risk"
  ],
